#!/usr/bin/env node
// Stub of `claude` for the ct-next.mjs tests (D4). It exists ONLY so that the
// precondition search (`findInPath('claude')`, which does statSync +
// accessSync and NEVER runs anything) finds an executable deterministically,
// without depending on whether the machine running the tests has `claude`
// installed, or on where.
//
// If this ever gets EXECUTED, it is a bug: nothing in ct-next.mjs should
// launch `claude` — the login shell that cmux opens launches it, inside a real
// session. The exit code 97 is deliberately odd so that it stands out in a
// test's output if it ever happens.
console.error('fake-claude: este stub NUNCA debe ejecutarse — ct-next.mjs solo debe BUSCAR claude en el PATH, no invocarlo.')
process.exit(97)
